sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor ClientA as Stale Client A
    actor ClientB as New Client B
    participant LG as LockGuard Cluster
    participant PR as Protected Resource Service
    participant Storage as Protected Storage / Database

    ClientA->>LG: Acquire("critical-record")
    LG-->>ClientA: Granted (FencingToken=4, TTL=10s)
    
    Note over ClientA: GC Pause / Network Partition / CPU Stall (>10s)
    Note over LG: Lock expires due to heartbeat / lease timeout

    ClientB->>LG: Acquire("critical-record")
    LG-->>ClientB: Granted (FencingToken=5, TTL=10s)

    ClientB->>PR: POST /mutate {token: 5, data: "Update B"}
    Note over PR: Check token (5) > highest_seen (0)
    PR->>Storage: Apply Update B
    PR->>PR: Record highest_seen = 5
    PR-->>ClientB: HTTP 200 OK (Mutated)

    Note over ClientA: Client A wakes up from stall (believes it owns lock)
    ClientA->>PR: POST /mutate {token: 4, data: "Update A"}
    Note over PR: Check token (4) <= highest_seen (5)
    Note over PR: STALE FENCING TOKEN DETECTED!
    PR--xStorage: Reject Mutation (Prevent Data Corruption)
    PR-->>ClientA: HTTP 409 Conflict {error: "ERR_STALE_FENCING_TOKEN", max_token: 5}

